Title: F2-M04 — Stone Bridge (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. WEST ABUTMENT DUGOUT - GREY DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: river running fast below, wind in the arch, detonator wire being paid out]]
[[MUSIC: slow, heavy brass under tension]]

A sketch of the bridge piers is weighted down with rifle cartridges. COMMANDER SAVA and ENGINEER KOVAC stand over it. Kovac's detonator case is open.

COMMANDER SAVA
(serious)
The stone bridge is old, but it carries the only road wide enough for their armour. Command wants it held. I want it gone.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: river north–south, stone bridge with three crossing cells, west ramp with bunker sites, observation hill on the east bank, east road where the enemy column stages, artillery park to the north]]

ENGINEER KOVAC
(calculating)
Four piers. Eighteen minutes to cut and set them. Not seventeen fifty. I need two observers on that hill across the river to see the charges go, or I am guessing.

ENGINEER KOVAC
(measured)
I can bring it down cleanly, but I need time and an observation post to call the charges.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
The risk is the ramp. Everything they send has to come through three cells of bridge. If the bunkers and the gun team hold the ramp, their armour dies in a line. If they do not, it dies on top of you.

ENGINEER KOVAC
Waves every hundred and fifty seconds, by my count of their last probe. Tighter later. My crew does not stop for shelling, Commander; it stops for being dead.

COMMANDER SAVA
(firm)
Hold the riverbank, secure the hill, and protect the engineers until the bridge is destroyed.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
They have guns of their own north of the river. If they ever stop aiming at the ramp, find out what they are aiming at instead.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
